<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Na Gbewaa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Na Gbewaa is the founding ancestor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mole-dagbani">Mole-Dagbani</a> kingdoms of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a> in oral tradition, said to have settled at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pusiga">Pusiga</a>, probably in the 14th or 15th century. His sons and grandsons are credited with founding Mamprugu, Dagbon and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanumba">Nanumba</a>, and through a daughter the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mossi">Mossi</a> kingdoms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burkina-faso">Burkina Faso</a> trace their royal descent from him.</p></div>
